{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/869081-solar-role-charms","id":869081,"title":"Solar Role Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-19T21:03:30-07:00","id":869081,"title":"Solar Role Charms","content":"So a few months or so ago I had this idea for a character who was kind of like a Creation version of an Adeptus administratum official. Basically he's got two retainers that carry around his massive fucking book that might as well say &quot;Da Rules&quot; on it and he leverages the massive power of the bureaucracy to his advantage. If you want to deny him access to your records, or tell him he can't rent you a ship he flips the book open to Chapter 4.2, secton 1, paragraph a, sub-paragraph (j) which has this terribly specific little rule that would make things very very hard for you. He'd use this to duck superiors, leverage people, get places he wasn't supposed to, and in emergencies he'd pull out the short daiklave hidden in the spine of the book and kick some ass. He's just a small cog in a big machine, but he uses that to his advantage. After all, you can argue with the boss, but you can't argue with &quot;I'm sorry sir, it's the rules. Take it up with management if you have a problem. Now in the mean time let me past and give me your helmet.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, the Solar charms don't really do a lot of that kind of stuff and I wonder if it's by design. Some of the bureaucracy charms don't even function if you're a little cog in a big machine, they only really work when you're da-boss.That got me thinking, what other areas are there that Solars don't really go because of their inherent &quot;I'm the big important hero here.&quot; style. Giving quiet advice?<br /> <br /> Solars certainly can give advice, but they seem to be a lot more like the Avatar from Last Airbender, where their advice is more of a prophetic warning with a huge weight to it, and less a friendly whisper from the dude behind the throne. Getting bonuses from being subservient as well, for example I don't see a Solar charm getting free dice if they're acting under orders from a superior. Or maybe a charm that specifically only works when they're working under somebody, or retracing lore or crafts from a long ago master.<br /> <br /> Solars are kind of the frontline fighters, the kings, the prophets, the generals, the champions, the savants. That leaves a lot of room for the advisors, apprentices, retainers, squires, ect. Obviously there's a lot Solars can do that aren't covered by charms, but am I just seeing an omission of boring effects, or a design choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T21:24:12-07:00","id":869092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/869081-solar-role-charms#post869081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the Solar charms don't really do a lot of that kind of stuff and I wonder if it's by design. Some of the bureaucracy charms don't even function if you're a little cog in a big machine, they only really work when you're da-boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should work. You can always structure the organization so that the Solar is in charge of a significant branch of it so that they can use most of their charms, but not high enough to be calling the shot. I imagine most Solar Guildsmen will be in charge of their own business, but they won't have a seat at the Hierarchs' table, and they'd certainly be able to use their Bureaucracy charms. <br /> <br /> For everything else... I guess it depends on what kind of character you're playing? Solars are naturally better, so it's normal for them to gravitate towards positions of leadership in any meritocracy, but if you play a character with low social abilities - or social abilities that don't lend themselves to managing groups - or a character who's hyper-focused and doesn't have access to secondary abilities that support their given profession, you'd be more likely to fill a support role. It's kind of like Doctor Strange. You might be the greatest medical practitioner in Creation, but you won't be performing surgeries if you have Dexterity 1. Just apply that to different professions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T07:52:58-07:00","id":869313,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough, I think your character's description could be pretty easily pulled off as a Presence character. It's so often associated with &quot;mind control&quot; that we sometimes forget it's supposed to be &quot;the force of my presence causes you to believe what I say&quot; and what you're saying is they have to follow the rules, it's written right goddamn here!<br /> <br /> I get what you're saying though, you don't want Bureaucracy flavoring on a difference charmset. I'm just suggesting, it wouldn't take much to pull that off with Presence backed by Bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:56:38-07:00","id":869360,"title":"","content":"I think it's a design choice myself. Sidereals are the bureaucrats, schemers, powers behind the throne, and quiet advisers, so their charms reflect that, while Solars are the God Kings of Legend and their charms reflect that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:10:19-07:00","id":869368,"title":"","content":"Presence and Thrown charms. Literally throw the rule book at them!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/869081-solar-role-charms?p=869360#post869360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a design choice myself. Sidereals are the bureaucrats, schemers, powers behind the throne, and quiet advisers, so their charms reflect that, while Solars are the God Kings of Legend and their charms reflect that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pleases me both as a Sidereal and Solar player.<br /> <br /> I have a Solar NPC concept of a Thousand Scales Bureaucrat turned Eclipse. He has a family, so he need to stay hidden and pass as a Mortal. This is VERY difficult for him - he has to practice great self control at each decision his Dragonblooded boss makes. As a Solar, he could run this department (and the entire Scarlet Empire to be honest) so much better! I haven't figured out what his outlet for Essence Fever is because he has to have one or else he'd go fucking nuts. Or not have one and have him limit break.<br /> <br /> Anywho, the whole concept is based on how difficult it is for a Solar to hide in the shadows of another. It should be difficult for a Solar to play a mild mannered assistant to a Dragonblooded and I am glad the charm set doesn't really support this concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 04-20-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:15:34-07:00","id":869375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/869081-solar-role-charms?p=869368#post869368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presence and Thrown charms. Literally throw the rule book at them!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This pleases me both as a Sidereal and Solar player.<br /> <br /> I have a Solar NPC concept of a Thousand Scales Bureaucrat turned Eclipse. He has a family, so he need to stay hidden and pass as a Mortal. This is VERY difficult for him - he has to practice great self control at each decision his Dragonblooded boss makes. As a Solar, he could run this department (and the entire Scarlet Empire to be honest) so much better! I haven't figured out what his outlet for Essence Fever is because he has to have one or else he'd go fucking nuts. Or not have one and have him limit break.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Exaltion is the Second Breath, then Essence Fever is the Second Puberty in my mind. You don't really have a single &quot;outlet&quot; so much as various ways your Exalt is driven by their passions.<br /> <br /> (It's the justification for the usually hasty decisions PCs like to make in the games I play. Don't worry too much about it and if the time comes in game for the opportunity, take it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:19:49-07:00","id":869409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/869081-solar-role-charms#post869081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a few months or so ago I had this idea for a character who was kind of like a Creation version of an Adeptus administratum official. Basically he's got two retainers that carry around his massive fucking book that might as well say &quot;Da Rules&quot; on it and he leverages the massive power of the bureaucracy to his advantage. If you want to deny him access to your records, or tell him he can't rent you a ship he flips the book open to Chapter 4.2, secton 1, paragraph a, sub-paragraph (j) which has this terribly specific little rule that would make things very very hard for you. He'd use this to duck superiors, leverage people, get places he wasn't supposed to, and in emergencies he'd pull out the short daiklave hidden in the spine of the book and kick some ass. He's just a small cog in a big machine, but he uses that to his advantage. After all, you can argue with the boss, but you can't argue with &quot;I'm sorry sir, it's the rules. Take it up with management if you have a problem. Now in the mean time let me past and give me your helmet.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, the Solar charms don't really do a lot of that kind of stuff and I wonder if it's by design. Some of the bureaucracy charms don't even function if you're a little cog in a big machine, they only really work when you're da-boss.That got me thinking, what other areas are there that Solars don't really go because of their inherent &quot;I'm the big important hero here.&quot; style. Giving quiet advice?<br /> <br /> Solars certainly can give advice, but they seem to be a lot more like the Avatar from Last Airbender, where their advice is more of a prophetic warning with a huge weight to it, and less a friendly whisper from the dude behind the throne. Getting bonuses from being subservient as well, for example I don't see a Solar charm getting free dice if they're acting under orders from a superior. Or maybe a charm that specifically only works when they're working under somebody, or retracing lore or crafts from a long ago master.<br /> <br /> Solars are kind of the frontline fighters, the kings, the prophets, the generals, the champions, the savants. That leaves a lot of room for the advisors, apprentices, retainers, squires, ect. Obviously there's a lot Solars can do that aren't covered by charms, but am I just seeing an omission of boring effects, or a design choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a mid-level bureaucrat, really? They implement the rules as they exist, and perhaps comment to their boss if something isn't working right. For any given task in the rules, a Solar can have the Excellency, and thus do it quite well. If he wants to persuade his boss of the necessity of change, he has Presence charms to do that. <br /> <br /> To take the next example, what makes an adviser? They look at the situation at hand, formulates ideas, and passes them along to the person in power, perhaps going so far as to try to ensure their idea &quot;wins,&quot; and is implemented. Again, a Solar is very well equipped to do this.<br /> <br /> So, I don't really see this as a hole in competence, and rather a decision on what merits individual attention in the charm trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:31:04-07:00","id":869414,"title":"","content":"Another question is are all of these &quot;rules&quot; your character would cite to get around and into things be REAL rules that exist? Would his stating them create the existence of the rules? Or is he throwing mumbo-jumbo at them until they believe him? Because SOME of that lies in Larceny.<br /> <br /> The Larceny tree absolutely has some rules-lawyering charms, to the extent of &quot;I'm totally supposed to be here, I'm the auditor and you are expecting me. Also that's my spear you're holding, give it to me.&quot; Just because it's flavored to be a thief doesn't mean it couldn't just as easily be a bureaucrat (sometimes the distinction between the two is... blurry)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 04-20-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:37:43-07:00","id":869419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/869081-solar-role-charms?p=869414#post869414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Larceny tree absolutely has some rules-lawyering charms</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Spurious Presence, Preying on Uncertainty Approach, Clever Bandit's Rook.<br /> They're larceny charms, yes, but they reflect really well that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Maybe the ST could be convinced into making Bureaucracy versions of those and of Lore Charms that work with / create actual bureaucratic rules instead of faking them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T11:31:02-07:00","id":869466,"title":"","content":"What my intuitive response would be is that's stuff would seem right as &quot;Any human archetype up to 11&quot; (if that's what we think of the Solars as being).<br /> <br /> It's more subversive than I would think of immediately for Solars (they don't by default seem to me to challenge or subvert the idea that the big, obvious, heroic, important, inspiring, mythic looking guy is actually as important as he looks, so much as play to it, even though yes, that heroic guy can be secret, not so much hiding in plain sight, or innocuous and plain). But, not verboten, to me.<br /> <br /> The only thing I'd try to intuit about why that stuff is lacking (if so, and if intentionally so) is that it might more pragmatically be a thing of nudging Solars' players towards high responsibility and leadership roles and away from being the second to NPCs and other Solar PCs (even if they actually hold power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}